{"Hardcoded dummy value 'refresh_token' is assigned to refresh_token when the token response lacks one, which will fail on the next token refresh cycle when sent to the OAuth provider as an actual refresh token": 0.9473299980163574, "The minimumTokenResponseSchema uses [z.string().toString()] as computed property keys inside z.object(), which evaluates to the literal string 'ZodString' at runtime instead of a wildcard pattern, causing safeParse to strip all properties except access_token and discarding critical OAuth fields like refresh_token, expires_in, and token_type": 0.852232038974762, "parseRefreshTokenResponse returns a SafeParseReturnType object ({ success, data, error }) but this result is assigned directly to key and persisted to the database instead of extracting .data, corrupting the stored credentials": 0.9643793106079102, "Zoho Bigin passes credentialId (the credential's database ID) as the third argument to refreshOAuthTokens instead of credential.userId, routing the credential sync endpoint to the wrong user": 0.9965611100196838, "The webhook endpoint guards on APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED but never validates CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET is non-empty - an empty string secret would pass the header comparison against any request missing the header, allowing unauthenticated credential injection": 0.5084039568901062, "prisma is referenced on line 96 in salesforce/lib/CalendarService.ts but is never imported or declared anywhere in the file, causing a ReferenceError at runtime": 0.9751148819923401, "Salesforce performs a raw fetch directly for token refresh instead of wrapping with refreshOAuthTokens like all other integrations, bypassing the credential-sharing mechanism entirely": 0.9636272192001343}